{"at": "2026-10-26T16:22:50Z", "by": {"agent": {"model": "GPT-6 Astra", "session": "tauceti-dependencies-2026-10-26", "tool": "Codex"}, "identity": {"id": "CBirkbeck", "kind": "github"}, "involvement": "unknown", "kind": "agent"}, "checked": {"choice": "checked", "convention": "checked", "edge-cases": "checked", "generality": "checked", "junk": "checked", "naming": "checked", "object": "checked", "vacuous": "checked"}, "id": "b442ddd28877adba", "kind": "review", "links": {"supersedes": "66af1228ca6037ab"}, "origin": {"kind": "file", "ref": "https://github.com/CBirkbeck/tauceti-reviewed-by-test/blob/main/evidence/records/codex-dependency-reviews-2026-10-26-25.jsonl#L1"}, "rubric": "ltb-rubric/1", "schema": "ltb-evidence/2", "subject": {"aspect": "definition", "commit": "b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53", "hasher": {"local": "ltb-local/3", "meaning": "ltb-meaning/1"}, "hashes": {"local": "d3e418765e5e9afb", "meaning": "3ce530c1843ae9d7"}, "module": "TauCeti.FieldTheory.GaloisGroups.Resolvent.Root", "name": "TauCeti.ResolventSpec.orbitQuotientEquivFactors", "package": "TauCeti", "toolchain": "leanprover/lean4:v4.36.0-rc1"}, "text": "The [bijection](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Root.lean#L425) with monic irreducible factors sends each coset orbit to the minimal polynomial of its evaluated invariant. The hypotheses require a monic degree-n polynomial with n distinct numbered roots in a normal splitting extension; independently, the resolvent must have no repeated roots. Here `≃` means bijection; `⧸ H` is a coset set, so H need not be normal. [Geissler–Klüners §5](https://math.uni-paderborn.de/fileadmin/mathematik/AG-Computeralgebra/Publications-klueners/galois.pdf#page=14) gives the irreducible rational case; the source’s minimal-polynomial argument works over any field.\n\nChecks pass: the [evaluation formula](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Root.lean#L451), [factor degrees](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Root.lean#L480), and [complete degree multiset](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Root.lean#L517). For X⁵−X, the [discriminant is −256](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Quintic/Collision.lean#L61), but the [sextic has repeated roots](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Quintic/Collision.lean#L85), [separation fails](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Quintic/Collision.lean#L124), and its rational resolvent root [does not imply containment in a conjugate of F₂₀](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Resolvent/Quintic/Collision.lean#L179). These are proved source declarations with incoming axiom checks; no local rebuild is claimed.", "verdict": "accept"}
