{"at": "2026-10-26T16:22:50Z", "by": {"agent": {"model": "GPT-6 Astra", "session": "tauceti-dependencies-2026-10-26", "tool": "Codex"}, "identity": {"id": "CBirkbeck", "kind": "github"}, "involvement": "unknown", "kind": "agent"}, "checked": {"choice": "checked", "convention": "checked", "edge-cases": "checked", "generality": "checked", "junk": "checked", "naming": "checked", "object": "checked", "vacuous": "checked"}, "id": "48a29e6c0a5c1e17", "kind": "review", "origin": {"kind": "file", "ref": "https://github.com/CBirkbeck/tauceti-reviewed-by-test/blob/main/evidence/records/codex-dependency-reviews-2026-10-26-25.jsonl#L9"}, "rubric": "ltb-rubric/1", "schema": "ltb-evidence/2", "subject": {"aspect": "statement", "commit": "b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53", "hasher": {"local": "ltb-local/3", "meaning": "ltb-meaning/1"}, "hashes": {"local": "759699ede4dcd0ee", "meaning": "a303eb51cb4b7ce9"}, "module": "TauCeti.FieldTheory.GaloisGroups.Discriminant.Basic", "name": "Polynomial.Separable.isSquare_discr_iff_range_le_alternatingGroup", "package": "TauCeti", "toolchain": "leanprover/lean4:v4.36.0-rc1"}, "text": "Here square means a square in the coefficient field; the right side says every Galois automorphism permutes the distinct roots evenly. Separability and the stated Galois splitting extension justify descent. The leading coefficient contributes a nonzero square factor, extending [Milne’s normalized criterion](https://jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/FT.pdf#page=48) beyond monic polynomials. Characteristic two is correctly excluded.\n\nThe [required controls](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/blob/4adc7e3d0b68a8bb9974126e7411667cb533255f/TauCetiRoadmap/PolynomialGaloisGroups/README.md#L769) pass at the reviewed pin: the [quadratic formula](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/SpecificDegree.lean#L130) and [independent quadratic parity criterion](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Parity.lean#L109); [even image for X³−3X−1](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Cubic.lean#L179) and [non-even image for X³−2](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Cubic.lean#L191); and the [`Cubic.discr` comparisons for the first](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Cubic.lean#L164) and [second cubic](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Cubic.lean#L168). The [characteristic-two theorem](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/FieldTheory/GaloisGroups/Discriminant/Basic.lean#L178) explains the exclusion. Registered controls are actual propositions with standard axioms and no sorry; the two anonymous comparison proofs were inspected in source. Additional checks: [leadingCoeff_pow_mul_discrSqrt_sq](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/b257e0ff255355b2b692c1311d061d2b4dc84e53/TauCeti/RingTheory/Polynomial/Resultant/Discriminant.lean#L622) pass.", "verdict": "accept"}
